-- title:
--   Wholesale repression reduces retail violence
-- statement:
--   The dissertation's central policy result (eq. 3.60–3.61): with positive equilibrium gross margin, $dv_a^*/dv_{ra}=\hat q_a\,d\pi'_a/dv_{ra}<0$, where $v_a^*$ is the equilibrium-violence function (3.57) and $\hat q_a=-v_r/(\ln q\,(\pi'_a+s))>0$. Repression aimed at the wholesale stage therefore reduces the violence generated by the retail stage, whereas repression at the retail stage has an ambiguous effect (the cutoff lemma). The best-response milestone establishes when $v_a^*$ is the actual optimum (the interior regime $\hat q_a<1$); at the corner the optimum is $0$.
-- source:
--   Gilberto José Nogueira Júnior, *Mercado de Drogas e Repressão: Efeitos da Intervenção Governamental sobre a Violência gerada pelo Mercado de Drogas numa Rede Verticalmente Relacionada*, MSc dissertation, UFPE/PIMES, 2019, Chapter 3. Eq. (3.60)–(3.61) and Conclusion.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_drug_market_model
import Definitions.Def_drug_market_equilibrium

namespace DrugMarket
theorem wholesale_repression_reduces_violence (q s t c v_r v_ra v_rb : ℝ) (hq : q ∈ Set.Ioo (0:ℝ) 1) (hs : 0 < s) (ht : 0 < t) (hvr : 0 < v_r) (hvra : 0 < v_ra) (hvrb : 0 < v_rb) (hmarg : 0 < eqMarginA q s t c v_ra v_rb) :
  deriv (fun vra => eqViolenceA q s t c v_r vra v_rb) v_ra = qHat q s v_r (eqGrossProfitA q s t c v_ra v_rb) * deriv (fun vra => eqGrossProfitA q s t c vra v_rb) v_ra ∧ deriv (fun vra => eqViolenceA q s t c v_r vra v_rb) v_ra < 0 := by sorry
end DrugMarket
